{
  "id": "warn-standing-owner",
  "type": "warning",
  "provider": "azure",
  "fixedBy": "pim-eligible-access",
  "title": "Standing Owner access",
  "summary": "Several people hold Owner permanently on a production subscription. Each account is a full-control target around the clock, including the contractor account nobody remembered to remove.",
  "notes": [
    "Owner can also grant roles to others. One compromised account can create persistence that outlives the original incident.",
    "Fix: make the assignments eligible through PIM, time-bound and with approval for Owner. Day-to-day work then happens with Reader or a narrow custom role.",
    "Keep exactly two break-glass accounts with permanent access, excluded from normal Conditional Access, monitored, and with their credentials kept offline."
  ],
  "docs": [
    {
